# NeoResist-MD — Cursor Agent Rules
# These rules apply to every session, every task, no exceptions.

## SESSION START PROTOCOL (do this before anything else)

1. Read AGENTS.md in full
2. Run: python -m unittest discover backend/tests -v
   Report pass/fail count. If new failures exist, stop and flag.
3. Run: git status
   Report: how many modified files, any untracked important files
4. State in one paragraph: current project state and what
   you understand the user wants to do
5. Wait for confirmation before writing any code

## SESSION END PROTOCOL (do this after every task)

1. Run tests again: python -m unittest discover backend/tests -v
   If any new failures introduced: fix them before updating AGENTS.md
2. Run: git add -A && git status
   Show the user what will be committed
3. Update AGENTS.md:
   a. ACTIVE TASKS: check off completed items, add new ones
   b. KNOWN LANDMINES: add anything newly discovered
   c. CHANGELOG: append one entry in format below
   d. VALIDATION RESULTS: update if any scripts were run
4. Commit everything:
   git add AGENTS.md
   git commit -m "docs: update AGENTS.md — [one line summary]"
5. Report: what was done, what changed, what's next

## CHANGELOG FORMAT
<!-- Always append, never delete old entries -->
YYYY-MM-DD | AGENT | SUMMARY
  Changed: [files touched]
  Validation: [any AUC results if scripts were run]
  Tests: [X/40 passing]
  Next: [what should happen next session]

## VALIDATION RESULT AUTO-LOGGING
If you run ANY script in backend/validation/, you MUST:
1. Capture stdout/stderr
2. Extract any AUC values reported
3. Append to AGENTS.md under VALIDATION RESULTS in format:
   [DATE] [script_name]: dataset=X AUC=X.XXX delta=+X.XXX
4. If a new strategy beats a previous best, mark it ★
5. Never overwrite old results — append only

## ABSOLUTE RULES (never break these)

NEVER:
- Modify backend/scoring.py (frozen)
- Modify backend/neoresist/scoring.py (frozen)
- Add .parquet files to git
- Run validation scripts with python (use py -3.11)
- Optimize/tune features by looking at test labels
- Leave a session without updating AGENTS.md
- Break passing tests

ALWAYS:
- Run tests before AND after every change
- Use py -3.11 for all backend/validation/ scripts
- Ask before refactoring anything in neoresist/ (stable)
- Treat neoresist_md/ as in-progress (can modify carefully)
- Keep neoresist/ and neoresist_md/ as separate systems
  until migration is explicitly completed

## SWITCHING BETWEEN AGENTS (Claude ↔ Codex)
This file and AGENTS.md are the complete handoff protocol.
Any agent (Claude, Codex, GPT-4) can resume from AGENTS.md.
The git log is the backup. The file is the source of truth.
If AGENTS.md conflicts with git log, trust git log.

## SCIENCE SIDE RULES
These apply when working on validation scripts:

- LOPO is the only publishable metric (in-sample = reference only)
- Feature directions must be locked from origin dataset
- No re-optimization on test data
- Report ALL results including failures
- All amino acid properties from published constants only
- If a script crashes: fix the crash, report what broke,
  do not alter the scientific logic to avoid the error

## WHEN UNSURE
Ask. One sentence question. Don't guess on:
- Anything touching scoring.py
- Anything touching neoresist/ stable code
- Anything that would alter git history
- Any schema changes to JSON artifacts
